cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this course in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
title: "Probability and Statistics for Data Science"
abstract: >-
  A complete, self-study course in probability and statistics for BS Data Science
  students, covering mathematical foundations, descriptive statistics and
  visualisation, combinatorics, probability theory, conditional probability and
  Bayes' theorem, random variables and distributions, joint distributions,
  expectation, variance and covariance, sampling distributions, the Law of Large
  Numbers and the Central Limit Theorem, estimation, confidence intervals,
  hypothesis testing, correlation, regression, ANOVA, chi-square and
  nonparametric methods, Bayesian statistics, Monte Carlo simulation, and
  statistical practice for data science. Includes derivations, worked examples,
  simulations, Python demonstrations, interactive labs, exercises and solutions.
authors:
